1. Project Overview
RefNet is a production-grade Job Referral Management Platform that mirrors how real-world referral systems operate at companies like Google, Amazon, TCS, and Infosys. It decouples the referral layer from the company's internal ATS (Applicant Tracking System), which is the correct real-world architecture.

Core Philosophy: RefNet handles everything BEFORE and AROUND a referral.
What happens inside the company's hiring pipeline after acceptance is the company's own ATS — NOT RefNet's concern.
This mirrors exactly how LinkedIn Referrals, Rooftop Slushie, and Teamable work.

1.1 Project Purpose
This project is built as an internship learning vehicle to demonstrate mastery of real-world backend engineering concepts including:
•	Distributed system architecture and domain-driven design
•	Stateless JWT authentication with role-based access control
•	Real-time bidirectional communication via WebSocket + STOMP
•	Asynchronous processing and event-driven notifications
•	Polyglot persistence (SQL + NoSQL together)
•	Production deployment with Docker and cloud infrastructure

